Embracing each other, you all finally give way to tears. It appears that only by a miracle did you manage to escape sure death. At last, you pull yourself together.
"Ok, we defeated him, didn`t we?" you say, trying to make your voice sound confident, "Conan, good job! What would we do without you?"
It is hard to tell in the darkness, but it seems that Conan blushed and he is trying to smile. You pull a blanket out of the backpack.
"Let's try to sleep now. In the morning we'll decide what to do next."
You don't have to say it twice; in a minute everybody sleeps like a dog.